  "essentialEvidence": "Official component membership, credits and perspective-choice rules for year two and the 30 EC graduation phase in year three, including the thesis credits, entry and assessment, for September 2026 entrants.",
  "officialAlternative": "The fresh new-curriculum EER and first-year Rules and Regulations are byte-identical to the previous official retrieval. EER Article 3.6 explicitly reserves years two and three examination components for the 2027–2028 and 2028–2029 editions. The old-curriculum 2026–2027 EER Article 1.1 applies through 2025–2026 entrants and phases out that curriculum, so its later-year components and thesis cannot be transferred. The Dutch study page and faculty announcement confirm the three themes, a second-year focus area with cross-perspective work, and a final-year thesis. The current course-repository URL again yielded a JavaScript shell. The newer admissions page contains 2027–2028 entry requirements, and the published minor menu is for September 2026 to January 2027. Neither supplies the later curriculum for the September 2026 entrants. Targeted official searches for the new cohort’s examination table and later-year progression returned no applicable allocation.",
